<title>CANADA: Thomson says no merit in opposition filing.</title>
<headline>Thomson says no merit in opposition filing.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thomson Corp chief financial officer Nigel Harrison said on Friday he sees no merit in the Lexis-Nexis division of Reed Internationa Elsevier's filing to oppose Thomson's acquisition of West Publishing Co.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not believe there is any issue in those objections that has not been fully discussed between Thomson and the Department of Justice and considered in arriving at the consent decree,&quot; Harrison said in a telephone interview.</p>
<p>Lexis-Nexis on Wednesday filed a motion in the U.S. District to intervene in opposition of Thomson's deal to buy U.S. legal publishing giant West.</p>
</text>
